*> HMAC-SHA-256 per RFC 2104. Keys over 64 bytes are hashed first; shorter keys
*> are padded with 0x00. The key and message are raw bytes, no translation.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. HMAC.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-K0 PIC X(64).
01 WS-KLEN PIC 9(3).
01 WS-IPAD PIC X(64).
01 WS-OPAD PIC X(64).
01 WS-C36 PIC X(64) VALUE ALL X"36".
01 WS-C5C PIC X(64) VALUE ALL X"5C".
01 WS-BUF PIC X(256).
01 WS-BLEN PIC 9(3).
01 WS-INNER PIC X(32).
01 WS-N64 BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 LK-KEY PIC X(256).
01 LK-KEYLEN PIC 9(3).
01 LK-MSG PIC X(64).
01 LK-MSGLEN PIC 9(3).
01 LK-DIGEST PIC X(32).
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LK-KEY LK-KEYLEN LK-MSG LK-MSGLEN LK-DIGEST.
MAIN-PARA.
    MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-K0
    IF LK-KEYLEN > 64
        CALL "SHA256" USING LK-KEY LK-KEYLEN WS-INNER
        MOVE WS-INNER TO WS-K0(1:32)
    ELSE
        IF LK-KEYLEN > 0
            MOVE LK-KEY(1:LK-KEYLEN) TO WS-K0(1:LK-KEYLEN)
        END-IF
    END-IF
    MOVE WS-K0 TO WS-IPAD WS-OPAD
    CALL "CBL_XOR" USING WS-C36 WS-IPAD BY VALUE WS-N64
    CALL "CBL_XOR" USING WS-C5C WS-OPAD BY VALUE WS-N64
    MOVE SPACES TO WS-BUF
    MOVE WS-IPAD TO WS-BUF(1:64)
    IF LK-MSGLEN > 0
        MOVE LK-MSG(1:LK-MSGLEN) TO WS-BUF(65:LK-MSGLEN)
    END-IF
    COMPUTE WS-BLEN = 64 + LK-MSGLEN
    CALL "SHA256" USING WS-BUF WS-BLEN WS-INNER
    MOVE SPACES TO WS-BUF
    MOVE WS-OPAD TO WS-BUF(1:64)
    MOVE WS-INNER TO WS-BUF(65:32)
    MOVE 96 TO WS-BLEN
    CALL "SHA256" USING WS-BUF WS-BLEN LK-DIGEST
    GOBACK.
